Ticket #4471 was marked as one known issue, but the export behind it contains **412 unique reports** across **two separate date problems**. The raw export has **427 rows** because **15 duplicate rows** overlap across export pages, so all counts below use unique report ids.

## Split recorded

| problem | reports | tenants | channels | notes |
| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |
| `parser` | 379 | 11 | app 204 · email 150 · form 25 | Shared parser reads day-first tenant dates month first. |
| `hint` | 33 | 3 | form 33 | `booking-v3` shows `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants, then reads the typed date as day-first. |

## What the merged ticket contains

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Tickets filed and closed

1. **Date parser reads day-first tenant dates as month-first** — filed in the public repo for **379 reports** across **11 tenants**, then closed when work on **#4471** was done in the desk's own system.
2. **booking-v3 date hint tells day-first tenants to type month-first** — filed in the public repo for **33 reports** across **3 tenants**, then closed when work on **#4471** was done in the desk's own system.

## Notes

- Intake tags do not split this cleanly: **23** parser reports were tagged `hint`, and **15** hint reports were tagged `parser`.
- Desk notes mark **5** parser reports as one-day moves, but their tenant and channel still place them with the parser bug.
- The current page at `/kb/incidents/4471` says the queue holds one fix. The export data showed two issues that needed separate tracking while #4471 was still open.
- After the split was filed, both tracking tickets were closed when work on `#4471` was done in the desk's own system, so no further repo work stayed planned on them.

